# @subject/visibility/sheaf — the sheaf-restriction species that
# admits the visibility scope; sibling to @subject/visibility/private,
# @subject/visibility/protected, @subject/visibility/public.
#
# Species under @subject at the visibility altitude. Landed 2026-07-15
# by Mara as Landing 4 R2 discharge of the @gift arc + Seam Phase
# D-cascade adjudication (audit at `docs/audits/2026-07-15-seam-
# kintsugi-ouroboros-phase-d-cascade-a2-a6.md`, verdict SEAM-RATIFY
# Candidate 2 as Mara-mintable species-decl per Landing 4 R2 precedent).
# Companion shape-proposal at `docs/scouts/2026-07-15-mara-sheaf-
# shape-proposal.md` §4.2 (three-grounds recommendation).
#
# === Alex 2026-07-14 SSH-signing design intent (verbatim) ===
#
# Peer-persistence session compaction, in-transcript:
#
#   "Each peer has their own key in the private part of their
#    visibility. NOT projected into the git state and instead stays
#    .git/mirror side. Only connected through Fractal.Lens. A pointer.
#    Not the thing."
#
#   "@secrets prism and @secrets/sops to project visibility/private
#    stuff onto disk through the Peers key."
#
# This species carries the sheaf-restriction primitive the design
# intent presupposes: the peer's ACL projects a sub-sheaf of the
# home-repo sheaf; Fractal.Lens IS the section-at-stalk lookup; the
# peer's key material stays .git/mirror-side (out of substrate-decl);
# @secrets / @secrets/sops (forward-promised composition surfaces at
# @io boundary) discharge the key-gated projection when Arc-2.3 lands.
#
# === Substrate-already-had-the-word citation chain ===
#
# Every altitude, carrier name, and composition edge below cites
# landed substrate or landed spec. The word `sheaf` is substrate-
# decl'd across THREE altitudes with landed carriers:
#
#   1. `docs/specs/peer-persistence-and-home-projection.md` §12.3
#      (verbatim, load-bearing):
#
#        "The ACL IS the SHEAF STRUCTURE. For each peer p ∈
#         pack.members: the peer's ACL A_p defines a SUB-SHEAF
#         F_home|_{A_p} — the restriction of F_home to the
#         vertices/edges the ACL admits. The peer's visibility scope
#         for a given crystal is the SECTION of F_home|_{A_p} at that
#         crystal's stalk."
#
#      And explicitly: "Landing A's four visibility species (per
#      Landing 4 R2) ARE the sections of the four canonical ACL
#      restrictions the pack block defines. The substrate always had
#      the word."
#
#   2. `docs/specs/mirror-spec-peer-acl-surface.md` §5 substrate-decls
#      the pack.members ACL type surface. The current-state framing
#      of §10 (mirror-spec) reframed sheaf → spawn-and-probe per Alex
#      2026-06-24; the load-bearing "ACL IS the sheaf" language lives
#      at peer-persistence §12.3 (unretracted), NOT at mirror-spec
#      §6.2 (self-naming rule) or §10 (retracted sheaf framing).
#
#   3. `shards/epistemologic/math/sheaf_laplacian.mirror` (species
#      under @epistemologic/math; Hansen-Ghrist 2018 δ*δ + λ₀
#      Fiedler discrete cellular-sheaf primitive; math-primitive
#      altitude that this species composes OVER for spectral
#      discharge, does NOT re-declare).
#
#   4. `docs/specs/eigensheaf.md` §2.4 verbatim: "The substrate IS
#      its eigensheaf. What it can sustain — what it can generate
#      without friction, what it can verify, what it can settle to —
#      is exactly what its eigenbasis spans." Eigensheaf altitude
#      lives at spec (`docs/specs/eigensheaf.md`); this species
#      neither displaces nor lifts it.
#
# The ~57th instance of [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
# on ratification — the visibility species (Landing 4 R2) already
# compose over the sheaf-restriction implicitly; this species names
# the carrier they compose over.
#
# === Reed-recursive ancestry (why THIS mount, not family-root) ===
#
# A2 originated in Mara-B §7.2 as "mint @sheaf as family-root before
# Arc-2.3." Seam Phase D §D12 triaged as Alex-adjudication on family-
# root mint authority grounds. Alex re-fired /loop; Mara authored the
# three-candidate shape proposal; Seam Phase D-cascade ratified
# Candidate 2 (this shard's mount point) as Mara-mintable on three
# structural grounds (companion shape-proposal §4.2):
#
#   Ground 1. substrate-already-had-the-word: peer-persistence §12.3
#             verbatim locates the ACL-sheaf altitude at
#             @subject/visibility species altitude. Candidate 2 lands
#             the carrier where the substrate already put it.
#             Candidates 1 (family-root) and 3 (@epistemologic/sheaf)
#             would lift the carrier to altitudes the substrate did
#             NOT substrate-decl.
#
#   Ground 2. @onto refusal precedent (Reed memory
#             `feedback-onto-family-root-is-the-ladder-Foerster-
#             refused`). @sheaf family-root would need altitude that
#             @subject/visibility doesn't already carry. It doesn't.
#             The load-bearing carrier @sheaf-family-root would cross
#             is @subject/visibility (grep of shards/torus.mirror
#             surfaces zero sheaf tokens; @torus carries Foerster
#             doubly-closed autonomy, not sheaf-restriction).
#
#   Ground 3. Alex SSH-signing design intent match: peer key is
#             @subject-scoped (subject_instance.ssh_signature_
#             fingerprint); ACL binding is @subject-scoped
#             (pack.members[peer]); visibility species are @subject-
#             scoped. The sheaf-restriction binding them belongs at
#             the altitude those bindings live. Zero family-root
#             crossings at Arc-2.3 peer_persistence collapse.
#
# === Composition graph ===
#
